From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christian Gmeiner <cgmeiner@igalia.com>
Date: Wed, 15 Jul 2026 12:37:46 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 22/57] panfrost: Add clip distance VS/FS lowering passes

Mali only supports perspective-correct or flat varying interpolation.
To get linear interpolation for clip distances:

- VS pass (pan_nir_lower_clip_distance_vs): Multiply clip distance
  store_outputs by position W after the viewport transform.
- FS pass (pan_nir_lower_clip_distance_fs): Multiply
  load_interpolated_input at clip distance slots by FragCoord.w.

The VS clip distance count comes in as a new compile input and is
recorded in the shader info.

The matching FragCoord.w multiply is also baked into the standalone FS
clip prolog so it sees linear values without running the lowering pass
on the prolog itself.

Signed-off-by: Christian Gmeiner <cgmeiner@igalia.com>
Reviewed-by: Olivia Lee <olivia.lee@collabora.com>
Part-of: <https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/mesa/mesa/-/merge_requests/40343>
---
 src/panfrost/compiler/bifrost/bifrost_nir.c |  4 +
 src/panfrost/compiler/pan_compiler.h        |  7 ++
 src/panfrost/compiler/pan_nir_prolog.c      | 95 +++++++++++++++++++++
 src/panfrost/compiler/pan_nir_prolog.h      |  5 ++
 4 files changed, 111 insertions(+)

